@startuml method2-Production
!theme cerulean
!include theme/method-theme.puml
title Les Petits Plats — Filtering strategy (Method 2)\nDeclarative approach using filter(), some() and applyAllFilters()

partition "Search engine" {
  start
  :query = normalizeString(query);

  note right
    normalizeString(query) — Runs the following normalization logic:

      ◆ Removes accents and special characters
      ◆ Converts to lowercase
      ◆ Removes parentheses and unnecessary spaces
      ◆ Goal: standardize text and avoid false negatives.
  end note

  partition "Functional filtering" {
    :results = applyAllFilters(recipes, query);

    note right
      applyAllFilters() — Runs the following filtering logic:

      ➤ Normalization:
        ◆ Relevant fields are compared via normalizeString().

      ➤ Matching conditions:
        ◆ matchTitle(recipe, query):
            Checks whether the title contains the normalized query.
        ◆ recipe.ingredients.some(matchIngredient):
            Searches for a matching ingredient
        ◆ matchDescription(recipe, query):
            Analyzes the description

      ➤ Validation rule:
        ◆ The recipe is kept if AT LEAST ONE condition is true.
    end note
  }

  :return results;
  stop
  note right
    ➤ Method 2 — Functional filtering
      ◆ Uses Array.filter() and Array.some()
      ◆ applyAll() as the core filtering logic
  end note
}

@enduml
